  "response": {
    "html": "<h1 data-chunk-id=\"e905f4b1-171c-4929-bc0f-525ea69c4dd1\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;border-bottom:3px solid #0d47a1;padding-bottom:6px\">Nebula Drift - Game Design Document</h1>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"ddf1e100-b665-4dff-84b9-c6e31731d63d\" style=\"background-color:#e3f2fd;border-left:4px solid #1565c0;padding:8px 10px;font-size:9pt;color:#37474f\">Vantage Nine Studios - internal - the spine. Numbers live in Mechanics; do not duplicate them here except as prose.</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"78431d2a-784c-4023-80a9-8d792053192d\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Overview</h2>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"09aee084-b2be-4bc0-8d8e-8a40785dd069\">Nebula Drift is a single-player momentum-platformer set in the wreckage of a\ncollapsed orbital shipyard. The player is a salvager who cannot fight most of\nwhat lives there and must out-move it instead.</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"8966c268-3d2b-4dbf-bf16-0126c4c3166f\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Design pillars</h2>\n<ul data-chunk-id=\"9b64c762-4adb-4d7b-9d71-92165409a061\">\n<li><strong>Momentum is the reward.</strong> Every system either preserves speed or\nexplains clearly why it took it away.</li>\n<li><strong>The wreck remembers.</strong> Sections the player has stripped stay stripped.</li>\n<li><strong>Legibility over spectacle.</strong> If a hazard cannot be read in one frame at\nspeed, it is cut.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"b3897696-a342-47e3-b981-f6013a7e5006\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Core loop</h2>\n<ol data-chunk-id=\"19394cef-9fea-4466-9f6e-5cf71eb691c9\">\n<li>Enter a sector and read its silhouette for salvage.</li>\n<li>Route through it without stopping.</li>\n<li>Strip what you reached; lose what you did not.</li>\n<li>Spend salvage on traversal upgrades, never on combat.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"06c53ef5-4930-4f8e-9bfc-db72fb9536de\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Traversal</h2>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"c9c72155-affd-416f-8b0b-3db6528af4a7\">Traversal is the game. The player has a dash, a wall-run and a grapple. The\ngrapple is the only tool that converts height into speed, so it carries the\nlongest cooldown in the game at <strong>8 s</strong>, and every level is paced\naround that number.</p>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"883206d0-a929-4e4a-824e-a6f45d530fe0\">Full parameters live in the Mechanics sub-document, section \"Grapple\".</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"5fe89b16-9697-4544-8ef5-b70c14d85296\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Combat</h2>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"414472cd-d833-4d19-9c47-bfc585a11d06\">Combat exists to make traversal mistakes expensive. The player has one\ndefensive tool - an overheat pulse - and no weapons.</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"5cc1af2a-5153-494a-b490-b027d5352e8d\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Progression</h2>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"b165343a-99ad-4c97-a8ea-d87f9b700d0a\">Salvage buys traversal upgrades in a flat, non-branching order. No skill tree:\nthe team has shipped one before and it cost six weeks of tuning for no measured\nretention gain.</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"fbded2bf-b1a8-449a-b1a2-e373c1d62373\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Art direction</h2>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"83b4849f-a191-474a-9296-3f1580785533\">Readable-industrial. Detail lives in silhouette, not surface. Full rules,\npalette and reference boards live in the Art Bible sub-document.</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"f4bad83b-94f5-4de9-88f5-cc143366b09d\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Narrative</h2>\n<p data-chunk-id=\"e69490da-350e-499c-a17c-ab159dc7afe1\">Told through the wreck itself and one voice on a dying channel. Beat sheet\nand characters live in the Narrative sub-document.</p>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"55fc9029-daf4-495b-b536-ed205f128cd1\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Linked sub-documents</h2>\n<table data-chunk-id=\"6e39411d-af8e-403b-9706-7a3407ca5968\" style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;border:1px solid #37474f;font-family:Inter , Calibri , Arial , sans-serif;font-size:10pt\"><thead><tr>\n<th style=\"border:1px solid #37474f;background-color:#0d47a1;color:#ffffff;padding:6px 8px;text-align:left;font-weight:bold\">Sub-document</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #37474f;background-color:#0d47a1;color:#ffffff;padding:6px 8px;text-align:left;font-weight:bold\">Owns</th>\n<th style=\"border:1px solid #37474f;background-color:#0d47a1;color:#ffffff;padding:6px 8px;text-align:left;font-weight:bold\">Sections in this GDD that depend on it</th>\n</tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Mechanics</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Every tunable number</td>\n<td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Traversal, Combat, Progression</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Narrative</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Acts, beats, characters</td>\n<td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Narrative</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Art Bible</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Palette, silhouette rules, concept art</td>\n<td style=\"border:1px solid #90a4ae;padding:6px 8px;vertical-align:top\">Art direction</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2 data-chunk-id=\"d2a7c515-a3b1-4763-9d71-884e868b3410\" style=\"color:#0d47a1;margin-top:18px\">Open questions</h2>\n<ul data-chunk-id=\"5ac2507a-afa9-4f60-a054-470128c03e7d\">\n<li>Does the overheat pulse need a resource cost, or is the cooldown enough?</li>\n<li>Can a sector be re-entered after it is stripped, and does that break pillar 2?</li>\n</ul>",
